    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">80 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Build it yourself: 90 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine coding case</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 40 of the LLD question list</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>URL Shortener (LLD)</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">The famous TinyURL question, asked as low-level design: classes, not data centres. You build pluggable code generation (counter + base62, hash with re-hash on collision, random), an atomic \"claim the code\" step that is safe under threads, custom aliases, expiry with an injected clock, click analytics, and a clear line between what the LLD round wants and what the <a href=\"{{BASE}}hld/d01\">HLD version</a> wants. Java, Python and C++14 code all run, with tests.</p>\n"
